{"group":{"id":"b21-f2f","name":"B2.1 face-to-face","level":"B2.1","mode":"F2F","theme":"sunset","moodle":"https://agora-eoi.xtec.cat/eoisalou/moodle/"},"school":"EOI Salou","today":"2026-10-27","sessions":[{"id":"b21-f2f.s5","anchor":"s5","label":"Session 5","kind":"f2f","n":5,"date":"2026-10-05","unit":"Unit 1","title":"","test":"","cancelled":false,"message":"","header":{"goals":[{"text":"Read and listen to a true story, separating established facts from the theories built on them.","status":"done","id":"omupva22tyzrtf.5"},{"text":"Use auxiliary verbs to agree, disagree, add emphasis and check information.","status":"done","id":"omupva22tyzrtf.9"}],"activities":[{"text":"2 Reading & Listening — understanding facts","status":"done","id":"omupva22tyzrtf.5","book":"1B"},{"text":"3 Grammar — auxiliary verbs","status":"done","id":"omupva22tyzrtf.9","book":"1B"}]},"blocks":[{"id":"nmuqzkwsrqujdw.0","section":"warmup","kind":"text","title":"","html":"","link":"https://as1-design.github.io/english-learning-activities/mood-check-in.html","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.0","section":"memory","kind":"text","title":"","html":"<p>What do you remember? Did you learn anything new?</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.1","section":"speaking","kind":"link","title":"Pronunciation drill: shadow reading, series, tongue-twisters","html":"","link":"https://agendaweb.org/exercises/phonetic/long-short-i-exercises.htm","linkLabel":"Part 2 \"i\" sounds","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"nmuqq5o2cyix2g.0","section":"speaking","kind":"text","title":"Ask me a question- Communication 1A","html":"","link":"https://as1-design.github.io/improvedlessons/ask-me-a-question-1A-communication.html","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.2","section":"activities","kind":"text","title":"Review","html":"<p>Kahoot -ed 1</p>","link":"https://create.kahoot.it/details/75b7a4e1-8c8d-456f-afb2-1964d9d8f37a?drawer=","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.5","section":"activities","kind":"activity","title":"2 Reading & Listening — understanding facts","html":"","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"Read and listen to a true story, separating established facts from the theories built on them.","book":"1B","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.9","section":"activities","kind":"activity","title":"3 Grammar — auxiliary verbs","html":"<p>Strange — unfamiliar or unexpected. “There’s a strange smell in the kitchen.”</p><p>Bizarre — extremely unusual, often in a surprising or absurd way. “The film had a bizarre ending.”</p><p>Odd — a little unusual or out of place; often milder than strange. “It’s odd that she hasn’t called.”</p><p>Weird — unusual in a way that feels unsettling, awkward, or hard to explain. “That was a weird conversation.”</p><p>Spooky — eerie or frightening, as if something supernatural might be involved. “The empty house looked spooky at night.”</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"Use auxiliary verbs to agree, disagree, add emphasis and check information.","book":"1B","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.3","section":"activities","kind":"brainbreak","title":"Brain-break","html":"","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/d/1LRsgRBydfitPfjgfJD7FSB5K22v2RLrt","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.12","section":"phrase","kind":"saying","title":"There's no smoke without fire.","html":"<p>If people are saying something, there is usually some truth behind it — used of rumour and suspicion.</p><ul><li>A restaurant keeps getting the same complaint online; the owner insists it is malice, but the inspector books a visit anyway.</li><li>A politician denies a story four times in a week and the press get more interested, not less.</li></ul><p>ES: Cuando el río suena, agua lleva.</p><p>The Catalan and Spanish use water, English uses fire — worth two minutes on why. Pairs with the unit's speculation and unsolved mysteries.</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.4","section":"wrapup","kind":"text","title":"Journaling / Exit ticket","html":"<p>Write down one thing you didn't know before today's class.</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omupva22tyzrtf.10","section":"homework","kind":"text","title":"","html":"<p>Grammar Bank 1B exercises (p. 221) (b)</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"1B","image":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/d/1toxP3Mic4lqQlJ1KlXJ2MZxmGEO04SzD","continued":false},{"id":"nmuqtf0lygn6p3.0","section":"homework","kind":"text","title":"Question tags (usage & activities)","html":"","link":"https://agora-eoi.xtec.cat/eoisalou/moodle/mod/url/view.php?id=89465","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"nmuwckik6nyi2c.0","section":"answers","kind":"text","title":"Grammar Bank 1B (b)","html":"","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/d/1Q7cwj93VgpLuAttNnAV_aKAIPWUZro6D","continued":false}]},{"id":"b21-f2f.s6","anchor":"s6","label":"Session 6","kind":"f2f","n":6,"date":"2026-10-07","unit":"Unit 1","title":"","test":"","cancelled":false,"message":"","header":{"goals":[{"text":"Use intonation and sentence rhythm to show curiosity, scepticism and surprise.","status":"done","id":"omuwce53uo2zow.0"},{"text":"Follow spoken instructions and take usable notes as you listen.","status":"done","id":"omuwcli3wfidey.5"}],"activities":[{"text":"4 Pronunciation — intonation and sentence rhythm","status":"done","id":"omuwce53uo2zow.0","book":"1B"},{"text":"5 Listening & Speaking — following instructions, taking notes","status":"done","id":"omuwcli3wfidey.5","book":"1B"},{"text":"Two-vowel jigsaw","status":"done","id":"omuwcntjjwa92k.0"