"link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"Distinguish the sounds /ʃ/, /dʒ/, /tʃ/ and /k/ in the words you use about health.","book":"2A","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"amv9v9a1rgxt96.0","section":"activities","kind":"activity","title":"3 Listening & Speaking — tuning in to key events in an anecdote","html":"<p>(b, c, d)</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"Tune in to the key events of a spoken anecdote and retell it.","book":"2A","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omv97eq79zto0h.0","section":"activities","kind":"link","title":"Vocab training: Waiting Room","html":"","link":"https://as1-design.github.io/improvedlessons/waiting-room-B21.html","linkLabel":"Open","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"omv97ig2nqcuzu.0","section":"phrase","kind":"saying","title":"Prevention is better than cure.","html":"<p>Stopping a problem before it starts costs less than fixing it afterwards.</p><ul><li>A GP spends the appointment talking about sleep and walking rather than writing a prescription.</li><li>A company runs a two-hour training session on passwords instead of paying for a data breach later.</li></ul><p>CA: Val més prevenir que curar.</p><p>ES: Más vale prevenir que curar.</p><p>A rare near-perfect three-way match. Note English uses nouns where Catalan and Spanish use verbs.</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"nmvf91n4hgz68g.0","section":"answers","kind":"text","title":"SB answer key","html":"","link":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cT1H3VgCyX7yyDKm4igV47O-xMZNTQci/view?usp=drive_link","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false}]},{"id":"b21-f2f.s9","anchor":"s9","label":"Session 9","kind":"f2f","n":9,"date":"2026-10-21","unit":"Unit 2","title":"","test":"","cancelled":false,"message":"","header":{"goals":[{"text":"Review the vocabulary to talk about health and medicine","status":"done","id":"amvf10excqi0cn.0"},{"text":"Choose between the present perfect simple and continuous to talk